on_date":"2023-10-29","session_datetime":"2023-10-29T10:49:00","session_id":"session_27","session_index":27,"source_sha256":"5ccfe315ae15db342cd5b23e2ba8e1373dfa915337a96bbc461e2f91fe864fc4","speaker":"Calvin","turn_index":5},{"dia_id":"D27:6","global_turn_index":476,"locator":"[S27T6]","raw_turn_sha256":"fd5b542da23aefa393b32adb8aefb3e3c2d9683342a7b73762048c9f990038df","rendered_turn_sha256":"12d1376b128cfbe6650f81b8a680a342f6627781e642ab5f52c7f16055122b25","session_date":"2023-10-29","session_datetime":"2023-10-29T10:49:00","session_id":"session_27","session_index":27,"source_sha256":"d441f5991ec5ce825c43b13c253fce19c0e0b17559d817d0022c4e1da85ec84b","speaker":"Dave","turn_index":6},{"dia_id":"D27:7","global_turn_index":477,"locator":"[S27T7]","raw_turn_sha256":"744ed2e8c379db525c2e481ea0901f92cecce1b21ab97449517e12f7c1869adc","rendered_turn_sha256":"51aeeab0e7b91e53e5fdb78abd7d2abe13a2bfcd042f8bb1c8231bc2322a2a8b","session_date":"2023-10-29","session_datetime":"2023-10-29T10:49:00","session_id":"session_27","session_index":27,"source_sha256":"30c34ece33a52fae451414d1a9eba944d5f82b36c8917c735160ae684b63a1a0","speaker":"Calvin","turn_index":7},{"dia_id":"D27:8","global_turn_index":478,"locator":"[S27T8]","raw_turn_sha256":"b135bd0c46057df40105f74eb692701b3a0540ac6f5d5562afcbf9b7aec2e770","rendered_turn_sha256":"f606909ecff493e4f4a08f06313193e5c5d71094557380dce629e97f777ca52e","session_date":"2023-10-29","session_datetime":"2023-10-29T10:49:00","session_id":"session_27","session_index":27,"source_sha256":"bf5d5c6cae6cfc25b62834fcaa6c2fada18301c3ca733f6efa7258b8d221342b","speaker":"Dave","turn_index":8}],"speaker":null,"store_id":"s3","store_snapshot_sha256":"983238fddc77a88ef4ae3d06b50bcfd25a429f497e89c6af4d9477cefca9cad2","text":"- On 2023-11-17, reconnected with Calvin (\"Hey Calvin, long time no talk! A lot has happened.\") and said he's taken up photography and it's been great — he's been taking pics of the scenery around his area, which is really cool (continuation of the 2023-10-29 thread, see below) [S30T1].\n- On 2023-11-17, shared a photo of a boat floating in the water at sunset (a scenery shot from his new photography hobby) [S30T3]; and, after Calvin told him about his inspiring conversation with an artist at his Boston gala (Calvin's side in the Boston trip and Music sections of /memories/calvin.md), shared his new vintage camera that he bought this month (November 2023) (a photo of a camera sitting on a table next to a plant) — \"which takes awesome photos!\" — Calvin: \"Do you use this camera for photos? They always turn out so good!\"; Dave: yes — \"this camera is very good, it helps me capture those special moments really clearly\" [S30T5][S30T6][S30T7]; Calvin: \"Having a good camera is key for capturing those special moments.\" and asked what Dave likes to take photos of (Calvin's message closed with a photo of a sunset with a wave crashing on rocks); Dave answered in a later message of the same chat (next bullet) [S30T8][S30T9].\n- On 2023-11-17, answering Calvin's question about what he likes to take photos of: being able to take good pics is key, and he loves capturing the beauty of nature — sunsets, beaches, waves — sharing one he got recently (a photo of a sunset with a wave crashing on rocks); Calvin: \"Nice job, Dave! That shot looks great! Nature's so amazing!\" [S30T9][S30T10]. Dave added it's incredible how much emotion and beauty nature can convey through a photo, and agreed with Calvin that nature can boost the spirits in tough times [S30T11][S30T13]; he also shared a picture he snapped the previous week (~2023-11-10/16) — a peaceful scene of a waterfall flowing over rocks and boulders — taken at a serene spot in a nearby park (Calvin: \"Wow Dave, that picture is stunning! Where was that taken? It looks so serene!\"; the park details in ## Parks) [S30T13][S30T14][S30T15].\n- On 2023-11-17, after Calvin closed the nature-photo exchange with a photo he shot in a Japanese garden (a bench under a tree with pink flowers), Dave: \"Cool, Calvin! Found an even better spot, with a bench under a tree with pink flowers - so peaceful. A perfect spot to relax and take in the beauty.\" — describing the same bench-under-a-pink-flower-tree scene as \"a spot\" he found, and Calvin: \"That sounds great, Dave! Can't wait to see it.\" [S30T17][S30T18]; Dave then shared it — \"Check it out, Calvin. It's really calming, I think you'll like it.\" — and the two agreed \"We will definitely go there!\" (a plan to visit the spot together; if it is the same Japanese-garden scene Calvin photographed, the two have found a shared favorite, though Calvin's photo is the only image attached to it so far) [S30T19].\n- On 2023-10-29, told Calvin he's been getting into photography recently — he's \"seen some amazing places and taken some great shots\" — and offered to show Calvin them (Calvin: \"Yeah, show me what you got!\") [S27T2][S27T3].\n- Shared two Boston photos with Calvin on 2023-10-29: first, a photo of a city skyline at sunset with a clock tower — \"Look at this magnificent sunset I captured on camera. It's truly breathtaking to witness such beautiful sunsets! The sky looks like it's on fire!\" (Calvin: \"Wow, that view looks awesome!\") [S27T4][S27T5]; second, a photo of the clock tower in the city with buildings around it, which he took last month (~September 2023) — \"got a great shot - it was stunning!\" (Calvin: \"Wow, that pic is amazing!\") [S27T6].\n- When Calvin recognized the clock tower (\"In your last photo, is that the clock tower?\"), Dave confirmed it is the clock tower — he snapped it at sunset and the colors were stunning [S27T7][S27T8].\n- On 2023-10-29, said photography helps him capture and appreciate the beauty of nature — \"It's been an awesome creative outlet and I'm loving it.\" (his appreciation of nature echoes his park walks — see ## Parks; Calvin: \"You're so talented, Dave!\", to which Dave said \"Thanks, Calvin! Your kind words mean a lot.\") (Calvin's side in the Music and Relationships sections of /memories/calvin.md) [S27T8].","text_sha256":"ccb307c536d9214230712edc8a6a00f11d122a8a03a3111c7300e8c4b594971c","timestamp":null}],"integrity":{"post_tree_sha256":"983238fddc77a88ef4ae3d06b50bcfd25a429f497e89c6af4d9477cefca9cad2","pre_tree_sha256":"983238fddc77a88ef4ae3d06b50bcfd25a429f497e89c6af4d9477cefca9cad2","store_unchanged":true,"verified":true},"metrics":{"completion_tokens":1003,"filesystem_tool_calls":0,"model_calls":3,"orchestration_calls":3,"prompt_tokens":28060,"provider_request_attempts":3,"provider_rounds":3,"token_usage_available":true,"total_tokens":29063},"model":{"requested_model":"coding","served_models":["qwen3.8:27b"]},"prompt_contract":{"derived_prompt_sha256":"60d0c608bdda6e13c46a9e6cbf4cd7cae4f7eea8d7fcd2d8a4f8f9bde415df7c","filesystem_tools_sha256":"1632a476feccd761a1c6d21c9d2962d0975632f50d6c96678d69427a7f973ed7","orchestration_actions_sha256":"115512fb955e8c7fca557e4b995c5bfd8717ca72dfb184810b04343bc595cd08","paper_prompt_id":"refind-stage1-plus-r3-curated-adapter-v1","paper_prompt_sha256":"20422063cc471ee1de75c38e4250e1a141a731ea2970786a6c715dc3c83cf7de"},"protocol_version":"shared-evidence-bundle-v1","question":{"conversation_id":"conv-50","question":"What type of photos does Dave like to capture with his new camera?","question_id":"conv-50-q154","question_set_id":"locomo-conv50-main40-v1","run_position":23,"schema_version":1},"question_sha256":"ee1b09528838ec0b8f9fcab7efe63c89a09a916b3786f07f4a9085e2e2ef67d3","runtime_contract":{"evidence_budget_limit":16000,"evidence_budget_unit":"characters","round_limit":4,"runtime_sha256":"90b104be69475ce8ebb6df70875f8fee136e43793a93d9dfeab5350202c4f917"},"schema_version":1,"search_actions":[{"action":"search_chatrecord","arguments":{"keywords":["Dave","camera","photos","photography"],"top_k":5},"event":"action","observation_id":"obs-0001","provider_round":1,"query_terms":["dave","camera","photo","photographi"],"result_count":5,"returned_groups":["dave